        ],
        "liquidationMechanism": "Any caller may liquidate an ETH Trove below the 110% minimum collateral ratio in Normal Mode. Stability Pool LUSD is burned against the debt and depositors receive the collateral; batch liquidation is supported.",
        "liquidationDelaySec": 0,
        "backstop": "The Stability Pool is the first liquidation backstop. When it cannot cover the full debt, Liquity redistributes the uncovered debt and collateral pro rata across active Troves according to the documented Normal and Recovery Mode rules.",
        "shutdownOrBadDebtBehavior": "Liquity V1 documents no global shutdown path. When the Stability Pool is empty or insufficient, liquidation debt and collateral are redistributed to active Troves; Recovery Mode below 150% system TCR restricts risk-increasing borrowing and expands the set of Troves eligible for liquidation.",
